[{:db/id -1, :doc/id "doc-ayatori-bench-coscientist-iteration-43", :doc/title "ayatori Co-Scientist Iteration 43 — M4 surveyed (no bigger host in the fleet); rows on full-data parameters (4801.5)", :doc/path "bench/coscientist-iteration-43.edn", :doc/body "# Co-Scientist iteration 43 - M4 surveyed: the fleet has no bigger host; the rows move to full-data parameters\n\n> Seeds: M4 (a host with performance cores), S26 (full-data parameters).\n> Judge: bench/benchmark.edn v2; rung :sf1-full.\n\n## Generate / Rank\n\n  M4. Every fleet node was surveyed for cores, memory, load and resident\n  processes: benjamin, joseph, simeon, levi, judah are all Apple M4 minis\n  (4 performance + 6 efficiency cores, 16 GiB); three carry a 2 GB\n  comfyui fleet process. The only larger CPU in reach is the owner's\n  workstation (M1 Max, 8P+2E, 32 GiB) -- at swap 13.1 of 14.3 GB and load\n  15-30 it is not a valid SUT host, and it is not ours to load. Answer:\n  the hardware milestone needs a machine the fleet does not have. That\n  is a decision for the owner; no experiment here can substitute for it.\n\n  S26. The IC parameter files in use were the official LDBC SF1\n  substitution parameters all along (99 rows each). Only the short-read\n  message ids were subset-derived. Now 999 ids spread across all\n  1,003,605 posts; the SUT gates on that set: 4,682 checks, 0\n  disagreements. The 64-slot row on the full-data set:\n\n    rung sf1-full  slots  threads  reads/s  upd/s  on-time%  thru/s   params\n      it.41          64     16      3328     1475   100.00    4797.0   subset short reads\n      it.43          64     16      3328     1475   100.00    4801.5   full-data        (3712: 76.2% fails)\n\n  A finding on the way: an idle SUT on macOS is compressed -- after 27\n  idle minutes 4.3 GB of the 9.8 GB footprint sat in the compressor\n  (ps RSS 66 MB); the /ldbc/meta call re-inflated it before the driver\n  read it. The residency rule cannot see compression that a run's own\n  warm-up undoes; every sweep here begins with one. Stated in the\n  receipt.\n\n## Reflect\n\n  - Two of the three things left on this rung are not engine work: a\n    host (M4, and SF3's 13 GB is the same decision) and the ACID suite.\n    The engine's own next step is the binding representation (S34) --\n    a factor of ~7 on the join-heavy reads, bounded by the host either\n    way.\n  - The number did not change with the parameter set; the row's\n    legitimacy did.\n\n## Meta\n\nVerdict under bench/benchmark.edn v2: row re-stated on full-data\nparameters (4801.5, same rate); M4 refuted as an experiment, handed to\nthe owner as a decision. Ratio to the audited No.1: 29.\n\nSeeds for iteration 44, in order:\n\n  - Owner: a SUT host (performance cores; >= 32 GiB for SF3).\n  - S23b: IC05 so INS5 has a covering read.\n  - S34: bindings as arrays inside the join.\n"}]
